--------------------- CableDyn Input File ------------------------------------
CableDyn driver deck -- POLYESTER mooring with the SYROPE working-curve model (dynamic axial stiffness)
-- The most complete synthetic-rope model: a polyester working curve that softens from the
-- running-maximum tension the line has seen, split into an exponential fast spring
-- (EA_d = alpha + beta*T) and a slow static strain. The EA column is `SYROPE:<settings>|alpha|beta`
-- and the BA column is MoorDyn's `BA_s|BA_d` pair. BA_d drives the slow-state rate and
-- BA_s multiplies that rate in the line force. The settings file
-- (data/syrope/syrope_settings.dat) names the original-working-curve table
-- (data/syrope/syrope_owc.dat), the curve type
-- (EXP), and its shape parameters k1/k2. Constants are the values of the CableDyn Syrope test on the
-- shipped owc.dat table. Single-section taut line (the basic Syrope path), ~2.5 % strain. The
-- SYROPE IC history (Tmax0 = 2 MN) sets the working curve the static IC is solved on; the line
-- starts in that equilibrium (~0.97 MN mean). Tmean0 does not enter the state (the driver
-- notes that it differs from the equilibrium).
